    "title": {
     "en": "Khushi's classroom"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Khushi reached school early. Sunlight shone through the windows and the classroom looked bright. She drew everything she saw."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "wood",
     "metal",
     "glass",
     "ore"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Khushi drew her classroom. Name the things she drew: table, chair, window, door, board.\nShe wondered where all these things came from, who made them and what they are made of.\nThe table and chair are made of wood, which comes from trees.\nThe hinges, nails and latches of the door are made of metals. Metals are extracted from rock called ore, dug up from inside the Earth.\nYou can see through window glass because glass is transparent.\nDraw your classroom and label the things in it."
    }
